WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.967
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEFL preparation.

2
00:00:05.267 --> 00:00:08.770
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:16.645
Unit twelve: Writing: Write an Email. Today you will write a clear, appropriate email that completes the task.

4
00:00:16.945 --> 00:00:19.725
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:23.714
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:25.841
Subject line.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.697
Subject line means the short title of an email.

8
00:00:30.283 --> 00:00:32.074
Write a clear subject line.

9
00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:35.475
Your turn. Say: Subject line.

10
00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.729
Subject line.

11
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:41.299
Greeting.

12
00:00:42.283 --> 00:00:44.712
Greeting means the opening words of an email.

13
00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:47.200
Dear Professor Lee is a greeting.

14
00:00:47.817 --> 00:00:50.202
Your turn. Say: Greeting.

15
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:53.928
Greeting.

16
00:00:54.683 --> 00:00:55.592
Request.

17
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.734
Request means asking for something.

18
00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:00.920
Make a polite request.

19
00:01:01.517 --> 00:01:04.401
Your turn. Say: Request.

20
00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.337
Request.

21
00:01:09.083 --> 00:01:10.119
Explain.

22
00:01:11.117 --> 00:01:13.627
Explain means to give reasons or details.

23
00:01:14.217 --> 00:01:15.647
Explain your problem.

24
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:18.868
Your turn. Say: Explain.

25
00:01:21.733 --> 00:01:22.943
Explain.

26
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.452
Closing.

27
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.914
Closing means the polite ending of an email.

28
00:01:28.517 --> 00:01:30.168
Best regards is a closing.

29
00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:33.389
Your turn. Say: Closing.

30
00:01:36.233 --> 00:01:37.072
Closing.

31
00:01:37.817 --> 00:01:38.934
Appreciate.

32
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:42.356
Appreciate means to be thankful for.

33
00:01:42.950 --> 00:01:44.752
I would appreciate your help.

34
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.886
Your turn. Say: Appreciate.

35
00:01:50.733 --> 00:01:51.839
Appreciate.

36
00:01:52.583 --> 00:01:53.747
Apologise.

37
00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.121
Apologise means to say you are sorry.

38
00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.763
I apologise for the delay.

39
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.536
Your turn. Say: Apologise.

40
00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.633
Apologise.

41
00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:09.152
Task.

42
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.637
Task means what the prompt asks you to do.

43
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.319
Complete every part of the task.

44
00:02:15.917 --> 00:02:18.465
Your turn. Say: Task.

45
00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.243
Task.

46
00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:26.858
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:30.436
Visal, what do you write in the Email task?

48
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:41.598
You read a situation and write an email in about seven minutes. The prompt tells you who to write to, what happened and what you need to include.

49
00:02:42.683 --> 00:02:44.265
What is a good structure?

50
00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:54.597
Start with a greeting and the reason for writing. Then give the details the prompt asks for, make your request, and finish with a polite closing and your name.

51
00:02:55.683 --> 00:02:57.253
How do I choose the tone?

52
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:08.224
Use a polite, formal tone for a professor or manager, and a friendlier tone for a classmate. Address every point in the prompt, or you lose marks.

53
00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.855
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.717 --> 00:03:16.131
Grammar focus: Strategy: greeting, purpose, details, closing.

55
00:03:16.431 --> 00:03:17.641
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:22.172
Dear Professor Lee, I am writing to ask for an extension on my essay.

57
00:03:23.083 --> 00:03:26.827
I would appreciate your help with this matter. Best regards, Dara.

58
00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:35.330
Read the prompt carefully, cover every point, choose the right tone, and finish with a polite closing. Check grammar in the last minute.

59
00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:39.339
Be careful! Don't say: I start without a greeting.

60
00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.241
Say: I start with a greeting.

61
00:03:43.541 --> 00:03:44.833
Begin politely.

62
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:48.193
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.721
An Email to a Professor.

64
00:03:51.021 --> 00:03:54.077
The prompt says a student missed a class because he was ill.

65
00:03:55.067 --> 00:03:58.262
He must write to his professor and explain the situation.

66
00:03:59.267 --> 00:04:02.334
He starts with Dear Professor Lee and states his purpose.

67
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:06.900
He asks politely for the notes and apologises for the absence.

68
00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.190
He ends with Best regards and his name.

69
00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:15.313
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.126
An email should begin with a blank.

71
00:04:18.426 --> 00:04:22.440
A, greeting. B, closing. C, signature only.

72
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.674
The answer is A: greeting.

73
00:04:28.817 --> 00:04:31.025
To a professor, use a blank tone.

74
00:04:31.325 --> 00:04:34.584
A, rude. B, formal. C, slang.

75
00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.040
The answer is B: formal.

76
00:04:41.183 --> 00:04:42.684
Which phrase is polite?

77
00:04:42.984 --> 00:04:47.961
A, Give me the notes.. B, Send it now.. C, I would appreciate your help..

78
00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.486
The answer is C: I would appreciate your help..

79
00:04:55.650 --> 00:04:57.731
Why did the student miss class?

80
00:04:58.031 --> 00:05:02.149
A, he was ill. B, he was late. C, he had a party.

81
00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.013
The answer is A: he was ill.

82
00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.581
You should cover blank.

83
00:05:10.881 --> 00:05:15.567
A, no points. B, every point in the prompt. C, only one point.

84
00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:22.015
The answer is B: every point in the prompt.

85
00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:26.677
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:27.517 --> 00:05:29.621
How do you write a good email in the test?

87
00:05:38.417 --> 00:05:39.847
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:40.147 --> 00:05:54.099
I read the prompt and underline everything I must include. I start with a greeting and my reason for writing, then give the details and make a polite request. I finish with a closing and check my grammar before the time ends.

89
00:05:54.399 --> 00:05:56.120
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:57.017 --> 00:06:02.444
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: greeting, purpose, details, closing.

91
00:06:02.744 --> 00:06:07.068
Today's value is communication. Speak clearly and listen carefully.

92
00:06:07.368 --> 00:06:10.194
See you in Unit thirteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:10.494 --> 00:06:13.855
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

